  "_comment": "CONFIRMED live, 2026-08-19 — real captured response from GET /products/{id} (id 6a82c75d452f993158f1ae4b, the 'Test Product — Canvas Tote Bag' on the newer of the two Squarespace test accounts this connector has been run against, distinguishable by its Navy/black/White Color variants vs. the older account's Small/Medium/Large Size variants). Superseded the earlier UNCONFIRMED assumption that this endpoint returns the product FLAT, by analogy to create_order's confirmed flat response. It does not: the real shape is `{ products: [ {...} ] }` — the SAME top-level `products` array key as list_products' collection response, holding a single-item array for a valid id, and NOT `{ product: {...} }` either (the singular-key wrap get_contact's GET-by-id turned out to use). Also notable: unlike list_products, this response has no `pagination` key at all — confirmed absent, not merely unconfirmed. No fields were redacted; this is the full, real, byte-for-byte response body.",
